{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06JK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fb6ad280346362a580dd3b1ba5464da5eea3146f40ecf0a8f3a682476d6fa006", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6e8c782136e3bb5c8b467fb667bd9051e461a2334af93421ef82ed2c1b0ee403", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe deduce Schlessinger's theorem characterizing prorepresentable functors on\n<MATH_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0915a1281a6a02395685cbfe3749054d90f73e9bd1b3496ff338676bf6e4cb8a", "unit_id": "tag:06JK:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06JK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F, G: \\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\varphi : F \\to G$", "MATH_0003": "$d\\varphi : TF \\to TG$", "MATH_0004": "$\\varphi$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-minimal-smooth-morphism-functors}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:11f78c1604dbf1fd52a14c2bc799d539b75f93126a2126834b1fef0c18d71072", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4b6e823edc1df5ec754ce0c6aa18b369dc07008d88d02112ffb64a1141cf1f9a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be deformation\nfunctors. Let <MATH_0002> be a smooth morphism which induces\nan isomorphism <MATH_0003> of tangent\nspaces. Then <MATH_0004> is an isomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:844e535833de94187761b56cb6015ef22387a4a29b011d75efc3d6860453c1b1", "unit_id": "tag:06JL:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06JK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F(A) \\to G(A)$", "MATH_0002": "$A \\in\n\\Ob(\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda)$", "MATH_0003": "$\\text{length}_A(A)$", "MATH_0004": "$A = k$", "MATH_0005": "$F$", "MATH_0006": "$G$", "MATH_0007": "$n$", "MATH_0008": "$A'$", "MATH_0009": "$n$", "MATH_0010": "$f : A' \\to A$", "MATH_0011": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nF(A') \\ar[r] \\ar[d]_{F(f)} & G(A') \\ar[d]^{G(f)} \\\\\nF(A) \\ar[r]^{\\sim} & G(A)\n}\n$$", "MATH_0012": "$F(A) \\to G(A)$", "MATH_0013": "$F\n\\to G$", "MATH_0014": "$F(A') \\to G(A')$", "MATH_0015": "$F(f)^{-1}(x) \\to\nG(f)^{-1}(\\varphi(x))$", "MATH_0016": "$x \\in F(A)$", "MATH_0017": "$F(f)^{-1}(x)$", "MATH_0018": "$\\text{Lift}(x, A')$", "MATH_0019": "$\\text{Lift}(\\varphi(x), A')$", "MATH_0020": "$d\\varphi \\otimes \\text{id} :\nTF \\otimes_k \\Ker(f)  \\to TG \\otimes_k \\Ker(f)$", "MATH_0021": "$x \\in F(A)$", "MATH_0022": "$F(f)^{-1}(x)$", "MATH_0023": "$F(f)^{-1}(x) \\to G(f)^{-1}(\\varphi(x))$", "MATH_0024": "$TF \\otimes_k \\Ker(f)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-smooth-morphism-essentially-surjective}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-free-transitive-action}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{remark-free-transitive-action-functorial}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:bd091e32d4f81d362b33d01258d58e85cc329b50ee8cc543e4f476873395fedf", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:879848d0bb688210e0c05840aa1dc095fbc54b34ba5c2f96ee91fc392be8bce6", "source_text": "We prove <MATH_0001> is a bijection for all <MATH_0002> by induction on\n<MATH_0003>.  For <MATH_0004> the statement follows from the\nassumption that <MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006> are deformation functors. Suppose that the\nstatement holds for rings of length less than <MATH_0007> and let <MATH_0008> be a ring of\nlength <MATH_0009>. Choose a small extension <MATH_0010>.  We have a\ncommutative diagram\n<MATH_0011>\nwhere the map <MATH_0012> is a bijection.  By smoothness of <MATH_0013>, <MATH_0014> is surjective (Lemma\n<REF_0001>).  Thus we can check\nbijectivity by checking it on fibers <MATH_0015> for <MATH_0016> such that <MATH_0017> is nonempty.\nThese fibers are precisely <MATH_0018> and\n<MATH_0019> and by assumption we have an isomorphism\n<MATH_0020>.\nThus, by\nLemma <REF_0002> and\nRemark <REF_0003>,\nfor <MATH_0021> such that <MATH_0022> is nonempty the map\n<MATH_0023> is a map of sets commuting\nwith free transitive actions by <MATH_0024>.\nHence it is bijective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:23826984c23b02f8dc253dbbaa666099adea4bd0dad19a2ba585612edd724de6", "unit_id": "tag:06JL:proof"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06JK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$k' \\subset k$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d012609d04f3650f5a5489156f4762b92df28b31e6d2d64b6a21fe125d6164a0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b7bbd01a7782b5cdde14b815b7839193aa6de2e22111674efa92b3e7f92cbd18", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNote that in case <MATH_0001> is separable condition (c) in\nthe theorem below is empty.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:15d69605a229b693eeae498bcc46bf34693b6191c1cd87f8a63ed34a22c02998", "unit_id": "tag:06JK:prose-0002"}
